; pilot.inix -- recordWalk's first walk: the dialogs changed on 3 November 2026, under JAWS.
; Start with DbDo open on a table, RadioTrail if you have it. recordWalk brings DbDo to the front.

[about]
Title=Pilot - Select Columns, Filter Records and Order Records

; THE SAME START EVERY TIME (3 November 2026): the 18:49 run found the grid left on the standard columns from an earlier
; test, so every return to the grid read Sonic Radio's whole notes paragraph, over fifteen seconds. The walk first puts
; back the default columns, look's, with Alt+S and L, and then begins.
[step]
Say=First the default columns: Alt plus S, then L for Look columns.
Key=Alt+S

[step]
Key=L

[step]
Say=Alt plus S opens Select Columns, which says what is shown before its buttons.
Key=Alt+S
Hear=Select Columns dialog
Hear=Shown now
Hear=Look columns button
Wait=6

[step]
Say=Shift plus F1 says what Look columns does.
Key=Shift+F1
Hear=Shows the default columns

[step]
Say=Tab moves to Prime columns.
Key=Tab
Hear=Prime columns button

[step]
Say=Shift plus F1 on Prime columns.
Key=Shift+F1
Hear=Shows the primary key

[step]
Say=Escape closes the dialog and changes nothing.
Key=Escape

[step]
Say=Control plus F opens Filter Records.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter Records
Wait=5

[step]
Say=Shift plus F1 on the first button.
Key=Shift+F1

[step]
Say=Escape closes it.
Key=Escape

[step]
Say=Alt plus O opens Order Records.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Ordered now
Hear=Order Records dialog
Hear=Prime columns button

[step]
Say=Shift+F1 on Prime columns says it is the default order, by the primary key.
Key=Shift+F1
Hear=The default order

[step]
Say=C for Choose columns opens the two lists.
Key=C
Hear=Fields available

[step]
Say=Shift+F1 on the first list.
Key=Shift+F1
Hear=The fields not yet in the sort

[step]
Say=Escape leaves without changing the order.
Key=Escape
